      "order": 6,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "Small synthetic OME-Zarr stores, one per layout NGFF allows: a single plane (YX), a stack (ZYX, a Z slider), a time series (TYX, a Time slider with play), every axis at once (TCZYX), float pixels (contrast from the data range) and eight channels (at most six show at once). The last one, shape_yxc, puts the channel axis after the spatial ones: the ingest's NGFF check flags it (the orange badge on the viewer) and the viewer says which axes it cannot draw, instead of failing silently.\n",
